lies one must be more right-skewed than the other. Given the definition, neither lottery clearly satisfies the condition of having a greater portion of probability on unfavorable outcomes. Therefore, the decision reason cannot be meaningfully applied to this decision problem because the concept of 'greater portion of probability on unfavorable outcomes' does not clearly differentiate between A and B. However, if we interpret 'unfavorable' as the lower outcome (0), then in A, 50% is on unfavorable, in B, 0% is on unfavorable, so A has a greater portion on unfavorable outcomes, making A more right-skewed. Thus, under this interpretation, A is more right-skewed than B, and the reason would prefer A. So the reason can be applied: A is more right-skewed than B.",
